WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:04.280
and welcome back to Five Nights At Freddy's: Sister Location.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.120
Now, there's a few things that I wanna talk about

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.300
before we get started.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.260
Number One! These security cameras here...

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.500
Who's watching those cameras?

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.780
Because in the last one when I edited the video,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.740
Baby and her crew said...

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.580
'SHE'S watching us.' not HE'S watching us.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.020
'SHE'S watching us.'

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.220
So who is that, is that the voice on the intercom

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.680
Is the voice on the intercom actually Baby,

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.360
and is the Baby, those little voices in there

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.180
just the babies in there?

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.280
So there's a lot of mysteries here.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.880
Also this! *Dying baby sound*

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.640
Eeugh.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.560
This! (Squeaky clown horn)

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.260
This! (Distorted noise)

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.220
And this last one... Doesn't do anything.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:42.840
And neither does that.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.000
So anyways that's a whole bunch of stuff that's not important right now

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.020
We're gonna get back to Freddy's lil' room here and try to beat that.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.020
[Female Voice] Ballora gallery maintenance vent opened.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.100
[Mark] First, we got to get through Ballora

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
DANAHNAHNAHNAH

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:53.440
Ballora

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.100
DANAHNAHNAHNAH

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:55.880
Don't kill me

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.100
BANAHNAHNAHNAH

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:57.920
(Music box plays)

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.500
Sneaking!

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.440
Make it-

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.100
AHHHH

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.100
(Door opening)

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.100
Yeah!

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.380
Suck on that. Okay, so, I'm pretty sure my prob-

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.100
[Female Voice] Motion trigger breaker room.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.240
[Hand Unit] You may now interface with the breaker control box

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.100
[Mark] Okay

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.280
[Hand Unit] Using the interface may disrupt nearby electronics.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.620
If you feel you are in danger, feel free to disconnect the interface temporarily

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.060
until it is safe to reconnect

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.020
[Mark] uh huh.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.020
Okay, soooo, I think my problem here was, I tried to do too many at once?

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.920
(Steady electronic beeping)
Like, obviously, the danger is going to be... bad?

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.320
(Steady electronic beeping)
(Funtime Freddy laughs)

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.240
(Steady electronic beeping)
[Funtime Freddy] Well, hello again!

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.860
[Bon-Bon] Calm down,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.680
[Bon-Bon] and go back to sleep!
[Mark, extended] Hi!

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.620
(Extended) Hi!

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.080
HO, Okay!

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.740
He moves!

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.860
I did not know he moved!

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.580
Eugh!

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.380
[Funtime Freddy] Bon-Bon, say 'Hi' to our friend!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.720
[Bon-Bon] Go back to your stage, everything is okay.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.760
[Mark] Is it? Is everything okay? I don't know about that.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.320
So, it does save a little bit of progress

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.240
but I gotta listen for, the shuffle-y shoe of a- of a wild bear

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.500
[Bon-Bon] Everything is okay,
[Mark] But I gotta listen for, the shuffle-y shoe of a- of a wild bear

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.500
[Bon-Bon] Let's go back to sleep. 
[Mark] Oh Jeez

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.960
Oh yeah, go back to sleep, oh God, hi!

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.020
[Mark] How are you doing? Oh!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:13.620
[Bon-Bon] Oh, calm down!
[Mark] How are you doing? Oh!

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.880
[Bon-Bon] I think it was just a mouse! 
[Mark] GO!

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.180
GO!!

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.180
RUEHHHHH

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.040
Hup-

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.040
[Bon-Bon] Nnnope! No one is here!
(Mark grunts)

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.660
[Mark] Ha, ha, no one's here! Oh my god, that smile.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.660
(Laughs) That- That winning smile

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.760
(Steady beeping)
It's so nice.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.300
Okay.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.300
That's a shuffle. That's a shu-VRR

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.460
[Bon-Bon] It's bedtime! Let's go back to our stage.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.300
[Mark] I think

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.940
I think the little voice is Bonnie,

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.180
(Laugh-crying) but Bonnie is talking to Funtime Freddy

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.540
and that's not a happy duo!

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.600
Well it's happy for the-

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:45.840
GO!

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.200
[Bon-Bon] You didn't hear anything, silly! (Giggle)
[Funtime Freddy] I know you're over there somewhere!

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.400
[Mark]...And who's that voice?

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:50.900
[Funtime Freddy] Bon-Bon!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.900
[Bon-Bon] Go back to your stage!
[Funtime Freddy] I Th-think thats the birthday boy over there!

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.120
[Bon-Bon] Everything is okay. 
[Funtime Freddy] We should give them a surprise!

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.280
[Mark] Who- who's talking about Bon--

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.060
Who's talkin to Bon-Bon-

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.200
(High-pitched) IS THAT FREDDY?
[Bon-Bon] Everything is okay

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.920
[Bon-Bon] Let's go back to sleep.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.320
[Mark] Is that Freddy's voice?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.200
Why does Freddy sound like such a douche?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:05.940
And.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.140
AH!

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.220
[Hand Unit] Great job.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.080
This completes your tasks for the night.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.520
Please proceed back through the Ballora gallery with care.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.200
And we'll see you back here tomorrow.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.160
[Mark] Yes!

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.820
I did it!

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.660
I could have done that in the last episode

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.200
(Laughing) I didn't know that was gonna end right there.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.520
Woo!

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.200
(Exhales)

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:24.920
I feel lightheaded.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:25.980
(Door shuts)

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.280
....Oh god no.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.060
Oh god, not again

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.480
Da na na na na na na na nun.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.160
Sneaking.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.980
(Quieter) Da na na na na na na na nun...

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:34.800
Ballora.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.400
DA NA NA NA-

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.120
[Ballora] Is someone there?

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.940
[Mark]...nnnnnNNOOOOoo.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.200
Go back to SLEEP!

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.060
I think it was (laugh) just a mouse!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.580
[Ballora] I can hear someone creeping through my room...

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.600
[Mark] (High-pitched noise) Buh-- no don't think so.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.440
I think-- (Wheezes)

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.240
I think those appeared-- LIES!

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:04.240
eh

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.400
Eh

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.100
[Ballora] Perhaps... not.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.020
[Mark] Heh, yeah.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.780
That's the one.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.420
You don't need to worry about me!

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.740
I just need to worry about me!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.800
AND DON'T MIND THE YELLING.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.600
I YELL WHEN I'M NERVOUS.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.620
Okay.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.060
(Happy celebration music)

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:21.260
Oh!

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.380
Ooh~!

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.120
(Singing) /We did it! We're the best in the world!/

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.140
/And! We~ are friends! For--/

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:28.900
(Music ends abruptly) Oh.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.400
Ever.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.020
Okay. Anyway. I guess-

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.120
My friend song is over.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.900
Oh good- back to my soaps!
[TV annoucer] As the sun sets,

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.920
so also does another chapter in the saga of love lost

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.260
between Vlad and his distressed mistress.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.160
Can they be reconciled?

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:43.780
( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)Mark moans( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.800
Can their love rise again?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.220
That and more, happening now.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.760
[Mark] I- I, (laugh) I have no idea--

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.320
[Vlad] Clara! The baby isn't mine!

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.040
[Clara] It is, Vlad!

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.580
They had trouble catching him in the nursery today.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.260
[Vlad] So what? Lots of kids get hyper

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.020
and run around and stuff.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.980
[Clara] They had to knock him out of the air with a BROOM!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.800
[Vlad] ...I have to go.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.920
[Clara] They're going to dock your paychecks!

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.140
[Vlad] They can't do that!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.020
I am a vampire! I don't get paychecks.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.020
[Clara] You work the graveyard shift

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.480
at the Fry-Me Taco.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.620
Don't lie to me!
(Mark laughs)

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.660
[TV announcer] Ohhh the humanity.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.960
[Mark] Ohhh!
[Announcer] When will the heartbreak end?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.620
When will these two ships passing in the night

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.120
rekindle their long lost love?

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.120
Tune in tomorrow to find out.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.140
[Mark] My god.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.480
It's so bizarre because I imagine this is trying

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.820
to paint this guy's existence as a normal, everyday Joe

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.460
And he just- After he's done working he goes home--

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.980
[Little Girl Voice] Daddy, just once let me go play with her.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.340
She's so pretty and shiny.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.820
Didn't you make her just for me?

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.700
[Mark] Mmm...

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.400
Ok, so what's interesting about that is that voice

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.160
I believe is the daughter of Mr. Ashton. (Mr. Asshat)

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.340
[Hand Unit] Welcome back to another pivotal night of your thriving new career,

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.300
where you get to really ask yourself,

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.940
(Mark laughs)
"What am I doing with my life?"

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.300
(Mark laughs again)
"What would my friends say?"

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.880
(Mark laugh-cries)
...and most importantly, "Will I ever see my family again?"

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.160
(Mark cries)
We understand the stresses of a new job,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.440
and we're here for you.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.340
To help you reach a more stable and

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.240
relaxing frame of mind, we offer several musical

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.320
selections to help make this elevator ride as relaxing

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.360
and therapeutic as possible. 
[Mark] Aww.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.060
[Hand Unit] We offer contemporary jazz, classical,

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.380
rainforest ambience,

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.860
as well as a wide selection of other choices.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.740
[Mark] Cool!
[Hand Unit] Using the keypad below,  please

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.200
type the first few letters of the musical selection you would prefer.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.500
[Mark] Sure!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.000
[Hand Unit] It seems you had some trouble with the keypad.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.880
I see what you were trying to type, and I will

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.000
[Mark] Dubstep?
autocorrect it for you.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.340
[Hand Unit] Thank you for selecting...

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.000
Casual Bongos. 
(Mark laughs)

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.260
[Mark, laughing] Casual Bongos?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.460
(Casual bongos start playing)

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.620
[Mark] Oh yeah! 
[Hand Unit] Now that your elevator

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.880
experience has been customized to your needs,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.620
(Casual bongos continue)
and you're thoroughly relaxed, it's worth mentioning

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.960
that due to your lackluster performance yesterday,

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:59.220
your pay has been decreased by a substantial amount.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.180
Please enjoy the rest of your descent.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:02.260
[Mark] What?!

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.200
(Casual bongos continue)

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.040
These "Casual Bongos" have turned sour!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.340
How can you say that? What did I do?

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:10.020
Well, come on!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.560
Oh, also, Mr. Ashton (Mr. Asshat) apparently is a character in the books

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.020
And apparently...

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:17.980
That's Purple Guy.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.420
Whoever that is, is Purple Guy, but then that would make

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.400
Purple Guy the creator of this- these animatronics,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.220
so what does it all mean?

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:30.220
(Yelling) CAN WE CUT THE "CASUAL BONGOS?!"

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.220
(Huffs)

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.720
Is it gonna- is the bongos just follow me--

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.340
(Bongos stop)
[Hand Unit] Due to unforeseen malfunctions from

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.080
today's shows, your nightly duties will require you to perform maintenance

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.800
that you may or may not be skilled enough to perform.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.320
[Mark] Oh. 
[Hand Unit] It became necessary for technicians to

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.300
attempt to disconnect Funtime Freddy's power module.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.280
However, they were unsuccessful.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.440
Allowing them to try again would be an

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.540
inefficient path forward, as we would need to allow six

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:58.400
to eight weeks for recovery and physical therapy.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.240
You will need to reach the Parts and Service Room on the other side of Funtime Auditorium

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.140
to perform the procedure yourself.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.300
Let's check on Ballora first, and make sure she's on her stage.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.000
[Mark] Uh--

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.060
(Lights buzz as they turn on)
[Emphatically] UH!

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.740
[Hand Unit] Great. It looks like everything is as it should

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.260
be at Ballora Gallery.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:19.560
(Mark wheezes repeatedly)
Let's check on Funtime Foxy.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.780
It's important to make sure she's on her stage before entering.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:27.100
[Mark] Ugh! Okay, so this Foxy is definitely a "fuh-mail"(female)?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.480
But, you know, that's a revelation that's gonna have to

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.360
go in second place to what the fuck I just saw over on Ballora's stage.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:36.260
EHHH

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.660
(Lights buzz as they turn on)
Ok, never-- you know, never mind, maybe I shouldn't be so worried about it.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.500
Oh, yeah, Foxy's gone.
[Hand Unit] Great, it looks like everything

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.900
is as it should be in Funtime Auditorium.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.800
(Mark makes confused sounds)
There is no need to check on Baby tonight.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.720
Please refrain from entering unauthorized areas.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.140
Proceed directly to Funtime Auditorium.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.400
[Mark] I- Excuse me? Are you tryina' tell me what to do?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.460
How dare you! I'm'una go straight into Baby's room,

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.220
and check on Baby!

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:07.740
'Cos, if there's one thing that Markiplier is, it's a good daddy, and I'm'na check on Baby.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.020
Eugh...

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.740
Ok, so what've we got over here? Alright.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.800
Baby! Oh, boy...

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:16.560
I--

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.820
I don't think I should be here.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.340
I'm pretty sure I shouldn't be here.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.180
Is there any reason for this?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.160
Do I need to be here?

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.300
(Metallic clank)

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.600
(Metal grating)
Is there a point?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:29.900
Hmm...

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.860
[Circus Baby] Did you know that I was on stage once?

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.280
It wasn't for very long.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.980
Only one day...

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.020
What a wonderful day, though.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.920
I was in a small room with balloons and a few tables.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:50.020
No one sat at the tables, though.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.300
But children would run in and out.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:57.820
Some were afraid of me. Others enjoyed my songs.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.160
Music was always coming from somewhere else.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:03.800
Down a hall.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:07.280
I would always count the children.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.940
