Have you seen her make balloons?

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:39.760
Oh, Daddy, let me go to her...

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:43.440
[Mark, whispering] What?

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:48.320
What?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:49.800
What??

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:50.920
WHAT?

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:54.200
[Circus Baby] Shh. Be still. And quiet.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:55.400
[Mark] Why?

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:59.440
[Circus Baby] You've been sleeping for quite a while.

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:00.040
[Mark] Huh?

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:04.720
[Circus Baby] I think they noticed that you never left the building last night.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.380
The cameras were searching for you.

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:09.360
But they couldn't find you.

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:12.600
I have you hidden too well.

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:16.080
(Whisper) I kidnapped you.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:16.740
[Mark] Oh.

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:20.660
(Cheery music)

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:21.900
wHAAAAAT?

00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:25.460
HUUUUUUUH?!

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:33.200
What the fuuuck?

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:36.100
[Circus Baby] Don't be afraid. I'm not going to hurt you.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.300
[Mark] Uh huh. Yeah, sure. Okay.

00:23:37.340 --> 00:23:40.580
[Circus Baby] I am only going to keep you for a little while.

00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:41.520
[Mark] Why?

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:43.980
[Circus Baby] Try not to wiggle, though.

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:49.020
You're inside something that came from my old pizzeria.

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:52.500
I don't think it was ever used.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:56.240
At least not the way it was meant to be used.

00:23:56.240 --> 00:23:56.880
[Mark] What?

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:59.140
[Circus Baby] Too dangerous.

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:04.800
It's just big enough for one person to fit inside.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:08.100
But just... barely.

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:09.140
[Mark] Oh!

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:11.860
Am I in, like, one of those s-

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:13.780
[Circus Baby] You're in the scooping room.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:18.060
Do you know why they call it the scooping room?

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:18.700
[Mark] NO!

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:20.640
[Circus Baby] It's because, dummy

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:24.640
this is the room where they use the scooper.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:27.520
I thought that would be obvious.

00:24:28.580 --> 00:24:29.080
[Mark] Okay.

00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:31.940
[Circus Baby] Isn't that a fun name for something?

00:24:31.940 --> 00:24:32.500
[Mark] NO.

00:24:32.560 --> 00:24:33.500
[Baby] "The Scooper."

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:34.160
[Mark] Maybe.

00:24:34.300 --> 00:24:37.580
[Circus Baby] It sounds like something you would use for ice cream.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.160
Or custard. Or sprinkles

00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:44.320
It sounds like something you would want at your birthday party

00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:50.240
to ensure that you get a heaping portion of every. Good. Thing.

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:52.820
I wonder, though.

00:24:53.360 --> 00:24:57.200
If you were a freshly opened pint of ice cream,

00:24:57.380 --> 00:25:00.680
how you would feel about something with that name?

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:08.360
Thankfully, I don't think a freshly opened pint of ice cream feels anything at all.

00:25:09.380 --> 00:25:10.180
Uh oh.

00:25:10.660 --> 00:25:13.560
It sounds like someone else is in the building.

00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:14.260
Shh.

00:25:15.920 --> 00:25:16.420
[Mark, whispering] What...

00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:22.840
[Maintenance man 1] Okay, bring her over. Forward. More.

00:25:23.580 --> 00:25:25.400
Mooore okay, stop.

00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:26.720
Set her down.

00:25:26.780 --> 00:25:28.060
Waatch the step.

00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:31.020
[Maintenance man 2] What happened to it this time?

00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:34.740
Just seems like these things can't go a day without breaking down.

00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:39.720
[Maintenance man 1] Who knows? It's always the same, man, some kind of hardware malfunction.

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:44.600
[Maintenance man 2] Well, hey I have to be somewhere in fifteen minutes. This place gives me the creeps.

00:25:44.600 --> 00:25:49.640
Can we just get this over with? It's all automated. We don't have to be here for it.

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.300
Just get her on some rollers, then we can go.

00:25:53.880 --> 00:25:55.300
(Door closes)

00:25:57.760 --> 00:26:14.460
(Mechanical whirring, rattling, and banging noises)

00:26:15.760 --> 00:26:16.760
[Mark] HOOOOOH

00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:19.000
HOOOOOOOOOOHHHH

00:26:20.300 --> 00:26:21.760
OOOOOOOOOOOH!

00:26:23.020 --> 00:26:23.600
HEY!

00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:39.740
(Mechanical whirring, rattling, and banging noises continue)

00:26:39.740 --> 00:26:40.860
(Mechanical noises stop abruptly)

00:26:40.900 --> 00:26:41.400
Oh.

00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:43.760
Oh, Okay

00:26:45.160 --> 00:26:45.800
Ah, ahoh

00:26:45.800 --> 00:26:52.640
[Circus Baby] There's something very important that I've learned how to do over time. Do you know what that is?

00:26:52.640 --> 00:26:53.760
[Mark] No!

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:55.020
You gonna tell me?

00:26:55.260 --> 00:26:57.060
[Circus Baby] How to pretend.

00:26:58.080 --> 00:27:00.320
Do you ever play make believe?

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:01.260
[Mark] Tha- No.

00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:06.140
[Circus Baby] Pretend to be one way, when you are really the other...

00:27:06.380 --> 00:27:07.140
[Mark] (Whine) no....

00:27:07.480 --> 00:27:09.460
[Circus Baby] It's very important.

00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:12.980
Ballora never learns.

00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:15.040
But I do.

00:27:15.160 --> 00:27:15.660
[Mark] Huh?

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:19.820
[Circus Baby] They think there is something wrong, on the inside.

00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:30.260
The only thing that matters is knowing. How. To. Pretend.

00:27:32.240 --> 00:27:37.000
(Industrial beeping)

00:27:37.340 --> 00:27:38.300
(scooper starts hitting Ballora)
[Mark]: aaAAhh

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:39.940
ooOH

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:43.340
OOOOOOOH

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:49.960
[Circus Baby] I'll open the faceplates for you.

00:27:50.200 --> 00:27:50.700
[Mark] I don't want it.

00:27:51.140 --> 00:27:53.500
[Circus Baby] That way, they can find you on the cameras.

00:27:53.500 --> 00:27:54.620
[Mark] I doN'T WANT THAT!!

00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:58.480
[Circus Baby] Now all you have to do, is wait.

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:00.440
[Mark] AAAAAAWww...

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:04.360
[Circus Baby] I'd recommend that you keep the springlocks wound up.

00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:08.480
Your breathing and your heartbeat are causing them to come loose.

00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:09.600
[Mark] Oh, oh, oh, oh oh

00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:12.180
[Circus Baby] You don't want them to get too loose.

00:28:12.180 --> 00:28:12.680
[Mark] oHOH oH

00:28:12.680 --> 00:28:13.540
[Circus Baby] Trust me.

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:17.360
[Mark] oH OH OH OH OH OH, OH NO

00:28:17.380 --> 00:28:18.420
OH, Okay, okay

00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:20.020
Okay, How do I- Oh

00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:21.440
Okay

00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:23.440
(Clicking as springlocks unwind)

00:28:24.340 --> 00:28:25.260
I just gotta click and hold on em

00:28:25.680 --> 00:28:26.180
mmMM

00:28:27.460 --> 00:28:27.960
MMMMFH

00:28:29.100 --> 00:28:29.660
EEEEMPH

00:28:29.780 --> 00:28:33.620
🎵WHY IS BALLORA LOOKIN' AT ME? WHY IS BALLORA LOOKIN' AT ME?🎵

00:28:33.620 --> 00:28:35.180
WHY DID I WIGGLE SO DAMN MUCH?

00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:37.800
oh, hi, whO THE FUCK IS THAT??!!

00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:39.920
WHAT THE FUCK ARE YOU?!

00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:42.560
I'LL LOOK AT YOU IN JUST A SECOND, BUT HOLY SHIT!!

00:28:42.560 --> 00:28:44.560
(Minireena screams)
(Mark screams)

00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:45.900
aaAAAAAH FUCK OFF!!!
(Static)

00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:47.560
WHAT THE FUCK?!

00:28:49.300 --> 00:28:50.600
WHAT WAS THAT?

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:52.420
WHAT WAS THAAAT?

00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:54.100
What was that?

00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:56.280
What do I do? I dunno.

00:28:56.280 --> 00:28:58.820
Okay, that's all the time I have for this episode here.

00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:01.520
Wow. This is just wild.

00:29:01.520 --> 00:29:06.960
Like everything that I knew is thrown out the window, and it's all new stuff which is good

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:10.400
a-and it kinda ties together with something that I realized, that

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:13.880
you know, when Scott first announced this game and released the first trailer

00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:19.300
It didn't even have Five Nights at Freddie's in the name, if you look back at the trailer on youtube, it just says "Sister Location Trailer One."

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:20.960
And I think there's a point to that.

00:29:21.100 --> 00:29:23.960
We're not at Freddy Fazbear's pizzeria.

00:29:24.080 --> 00:29:25.120
We're just not.

00:29:25.120 --> 00:29:26.820
Like that's not why we're here.

00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:31.060
This is whole new experience. So I'm gonna continue this in another episode

00:29:31.060 --> 00:29:33.380
so thank everybody so much watching.

00:29:33.700 --> 00:29:36.500
And as always, I will see you...

00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:37.700
IN THE NEXT VIDEO.

00:29:37.700 --> 00:29:38.720
BUH-BYE!

00:29:38.720 --> 00:29:50.200
(Outro music)

